  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Diisobutylaluminum hydride (DIBAL-H) is an organoaluminum reagent typically used for the reduction esters or nitriles to aldehydes. </p><p>In the second step intramolecular aldol condensation reaction takes place. Cyclization occurs if the α carbon atom and the second carbonyl carbon atom can bond to form a five- or six-membered ring.</p><p>The Clemmensen reduction is a reaction that is used to reduce aldehydes or ketones to alkanes using hydrochloric acid and zinc amalgam. In the same condition, alcohol converts to alkenes.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3f811fdd-d017-402a-9d19-adbc42ba234d.png\" style=\"width: 671px; height: 410px;\"/></p>",
